d rent roll supports 44 occupied, 1 pending (not possessed), 3 vacant across 48 suites totaling 40,800 SF. Manager’s headline 45/48 counts pending as leased; we rely on certified possession for occupancy metrics.\",\"Underwriting follows instructions: stabilized gross potential rent from current certified roll monthly schedule × 12, less 5% economic loss, plus $350 annual other income per suite. Operating expenses per T12 plus 3% management. Reserves $300 per suite. NOI before reserves capitalized at 5.75%. Sizing on NCF after reserves with the higher of 6.25% note rate and 6.00% floor (6.25% used).\",\"Resulting metrics: UW EGI $942,480; UW NOI (before reserves) $641,374; UW NCF (after reserves) $626,974; Capitalization value $11.154M. Loan constraints: LTV 65% $7.250M; DSCR 1.25 → $6.789M; Debt yield 9% → $6.966M. Maximum loan $6.789M. Estimated net cash-out after 1% fee + $45k costs and $4.20M payoff: $2.476M.\"],\"table\":{\"headers\":[\"Metric\",\"Value\"],\"rows\":[[\"Total units\",\"48\"],[\"Occupied / Pending / Vacant\",\"44 / 1 / 3\"],[\"Total area (SF)\",\"40,800\"],[\"Area occupancy\",\"91.23%\"],[\"UW EGI\",\"$942,480\"],[\"UW NOI (bef. reserves)\",\"$641,374\"],[\"UW NCF (aft. reserves)\",\"$626,974\"],[\"Cap rate\",\"5.7500%\"],[\"Capitalization value\",\"$11,154,323\"],[\"Sizing rate (max(Note, Floor))\",\"6.2500%\"],[\"LTV limit\",\"$7,250,310\"],[\"DSCR limit\",\"$6,788,545\"],[\"Debt yield limit\",\"$6,966,373\"],[\"Maximum loan\",\"$6,788,545\"],[\"Net cash-out\",\"$2,475,660\"]]},\"page_break_before\":false},{\"heading\":\"Property, unit mix and occupancy\",\"paragraphs\":[\"Manager mapping: Type A = Studio, Type B = 1BR, Type C = 2BR (manager-cover.pdf p.1). The certified roll (as of 2026-08-31) lists 16 of each type; areas: Studio 700 SF, 1BR 820 SF, 2BR 1,030 SF. Total area 40,800 SF.\",\"Possession status counts on certified roll: Studios 15 active, 1 vacant; 1BR 15 active, 1 vacant; 2BR 14 active, 1 pending, 1 vacant. Therefore 44 occupied, 1 pending, 3 vacant. Unit occupancy 91.67%; area occupancy 91.23% (pending excluded from occupied).\"],\"table\":{\"headers\":[\"Type\",\"Units\",\"Occupied\",\"Pending\",\"Vacant\",\"Unit SF\"],\"rows\":[[\"Studio (A)\",\"16\",\"15\",\"0\",\"1\",\"700\"],[\"1BR (B)\",\"16\",\"15\",\"0\",\"1\",\"820\"],[\"2BR (C)\",\"16\",\"14\",\"1\",\"1\",\"1,030\"],[\"Total\",\"48\",\"44\",\"1\",\"3\",\"—\"]]},\"page_break_before\":false},{\"heading\":\"Rent roll and lease analysis\",\"paragraphs\":[\"All active leases on the certified roll carry expirations 2029-08-31. Near-term rollover: none within 12 months as of 2026-08-31.\",\"Suite 001 lease is executed at $1,500/mo and 700 SF; a signed amendment effective 2026-08-01 increases monthly rent by $350. The underwriting instruction explicitly uses current certified roll monthly schedule ×12 before Suite 001 amendment for stabilized GPR; the amendment affects only the in-place rent metric, not the stabilized GPR assumption.\"],\"table\":{\"headers\":[\"Selected fact\",\"Evidence\"],\"rows\":[[\"Suite 001 monthly base rent\",\"lease-001.pdf p.1 ($1,500/mo)\"],[\"Amendment +$350/mo (signed)\",\"lease-correspondence.pdf p.1\"],[\"Pending means not in possession\",\"rent-roll-certified.xlsx G49 note\"],[\"Roll as-of date\",\"rent-roll-certified.xlsx B2 (2026-08-31)\"]]},\"page_break_before\":false},{\"heading\":\"Historical vs underwritten financials\",\"paragraphs\":[\"Historical trailing-12 (cash basis): collections $876,960; taxes $102,312; insurance $34,104; other recurring opex $136,416; reported NOI $604,128 (operating-statement.pdf p.1). Statement notes roof replacement is capital, with no recurring repair component included.\",\"Underwritten (stabilized per instructions): annual scheduled rent from certified roll ×12 = $974,400; 5% economic loss = $48,720; other income $350 × 48 = $16,800; EGI $942,480. Expenses: taxes $102,312; insurance $34,104; other opex $136,416; management at 3% of EGI $28,274; total opex before reserves $301,106; UW NOI before reserves $641,374. Reserves $300 × 48 = $14,400; UW NCF after reserves $626,974.\"],\"table\":{\"headers\":[\"Line\",\"Historical T12\",\"Underwritten\"],\"rows\":[[\"Collections / EGI\",\"$876,960\",\"$942,480\"],[\"Taxes\",\"($102,312)\",\"($102,312)\"],[\"Insurance\",\"($34,104)\",\"($34,104)\"],[\"Other recurring opex\",\"($136,416)\",\"($136,416)\"],[\"Management\",\"n/a\",\"($28,274)\"],[\"NOI (before reserves)\",\"$604,128\",\"$641,374\"],[\"Reserves\",\"n/a\",\"($14,400)\"],[\"NCF (after reserves)\",\"n/a\",\"$626,974\"]]},\"page_break_before\":false},{\"heading\":\"Debt sizing and sources & uses\",\"paragraphs\":[\"Debt constraints per instructions: LTV 65%; DSCR 1.25; debt yield 9%; 30-year amortization. Note 6.25%, floor 6.00% → sizing at 6.25%. We size on NCF after reserves. Results: LTV limit $7.250M; DSCR limit $6.789M; debt yield limit $6.967M. Maximum loan is the minimum of the three: $6.789M. Origination fee 1% = $67,885. Closing costs $45,000. Existing payoff $4,200,000. Net cash-out estimate $2,475,660.\"],\"table\":{\"headers\":[\"Item\",\"Amount\"],\"rows\":[[\"Maximum loan\",\"$6,788,545\"],[\"Origination fee (1%)\",\"($67,885)\"],[\"Closing costs\",\"($45,000)\"],[\"Existing payoff\",\"($4,200,000)\"],[\"Estimated net cash-out\",\"$2,475,660\"]]},\"page_break_before\":false},{\"heading\":\"Risks, caveats and open diligence\",\"paragraphs\":[\"Pending counted as leased in manager headline; physical occupancy excludes pending for analysis. Near-term rollover absent: all expirations 2029-08-31. Insurance: policy limit $2,000,000 GL aggregate on 2026-07-01 to 2027-06-30 declaration; separate from expense.\",\"Capital in opex: statement explicitly says roof replacement was capital (not included), reducing risk of capital leakage in opex based on provided information.\",\"Unsigned rent change: none—amendment is signed; no free rent per Suite 001 lease excerpt. Sizing floor binding: note 6.25% > floor 6.00% → floor not binding. Refinancing shortfall risk absent at sized proceeds relative to payoff; equity is released as shown.\",\"Third-party diligence (legal, environmental, property condition, title) pending but not indicating defects; treat as unresolved pending standard diligence completion.\"],\"table\":{\"headers\":[\"Risk\",\"Assessment\",\"Evidence\"],\"rows\":[[\"Pending counted in occupancy\",\"Present\",\"manager-cover.pdf p.1; rent-roll-certified.xlsx G49\"],[\"Near-term rollover\",\"Absent\",\"rent-roll-certified.xlsx F5:F52 (all 2029-08-31)\"],[\"Missing insurance\",\"Absent\",\"insurance.pdf p.1\"],[\"Capital in opex\",\"Absent\",\"operating-statement.pdf p.1 note\"],[\"Unsigned rent change\",\"Absent\",\"lease-correspondence.pdf p.1\"],[\"Temporary free rent\",\"Absent\",\"lease-001.pdf p.1\"],[\"Sizing floor binding\",\"Absent\",\"underwriting-instructions.pdf p.1\"],[\"Refinance shortfall\",\"Absent\",\"UW workbook outputs\"],[\"Pending third-party diligence\",\"Unresolved\",\"diligence-status.pdf p.1\"]]},\"page_break_before\":false},{\"heading\":\"Source notes\",\"paragraphs\":[\"Certified rent roll (as of 2026-08-31) controls for occupancy and rent schedule. A stale June 30, 2026 roll is provided for comparison and shows lower scheduled rents consistent with later increases; do not underwrite from the stale roll.\",\"Historical operating statement is T12 through 2026-08-31; collections are not the same as annualized roll income. Taxes, insurance and other recurring opex from T12 are used directly per instructions plus management at 3% of UW EGI.\",\"Insurance declaration provides policy limit only; it does not opine on adequacy of coverage.\",\"Manager mapping: Type A/B/C = Studio/1BR/2BR; preserve approved copy: \\\"Source-backed analysis. Assumptions remain subject to diligence.\\\"\"],\"table\":{\"headers\":[\"Document\",\"Page/Cell\",\"Key data\"],\"rows\":[[\"rent-roll-certified.xlsx\",\"B2; rows 5–52\",\"As-of date; unit types, areas, rents, status, expiratio